      "report_date": "2026-11-16",
      "title": "Five Years Chasing Gootloader",
      "summary": "Operation Endgame disrupted Gootloader's infrastructure on November 12, 2026, as described in this first-person account by a threat hunter who has tracked the malware since 2021. Gootloader was traced to the Gootkit family and spread through compromised WordPress blogs that hosted malicious files and hidden SEO spam posts to boost Google rankings. The researcher reverse-engineered the backdoor's color-value scheme by brute-forcing hashes on a GPU, which let them identify many compromised sites. After an outside cleanup effort in 2022, the attackers changed the backdoor, making it far harder to crack. The author notes that many victim organizations were hard to warn and that some infections later appeared on ransomware leak sites.",
