      "title": "Malware Must Die!: MMD-072-2026 - ARTEX detection signature pack - from IOC w/playbook process",
      "summary": "The MalwareMustDie project released MMD-072-2026, a public, behavior-first detection pack (now v1.1.6) for misuse of the ARTEX AI pentest framework, an LLM-driven tool used in multiple campaigns from mid-2026. The pack covers Sigma, Sentinel KQL, Suricata, Snort, osquery, YARA, STIX and Zeek formats, and it targets web, identity, cloud and CI/CD telemetry. Because ARTEX indicators change quickly across forks, the pack treats IP and string indicators as short-lived context and relies on behavioral rules such as recon chains, password spraying, OAuth and application-credential abuse, and cloud secret sweeps. All rules are experimental and should be deployed in monitor-only mode and validated against local benign data before use. IP indicators are tiered as shared or past-incident infrastructure, with a warning against auto-blocking.",
      "completeness": "High",
