      "title": "CVE-2026-84869 in ScreenConnect Exploited to Run Malicious Files on MSP Technician Accounts",
      "summary": "ConnectWise's CVE-2026-84869 (CVSS 9.9) lets a guest in a ScreenConnect session trigger file transfers that the technician's host client runs without prompt or confirmation, including with elevated rights. Huntress observed attackers spraying MSP ScreenConnect servers with hundreds of thousands of \"run file\" requests for update.bat-style files, waiting for technicians to join. On November 12, one technician's workstation was fully compromised within about 9 seconds, after which a rebranded ScreenConnect client named WindowsUpdate.WindowsClient.exe connected to the attacker's relay. Other activity included canary tests, path traversal attempts into technicians' Startup folders, and near-misses. Defenders should update host clients to 26.6.5 or later, or remove the TransferFiles permission as an interim step.",
