      "title": "Poisoned Scripts on BBC, Zoom and Other Major Websites Linked to iPhone Exploit Loaders",
      "summary": "Poisoned third-party Optimizely, Kissmetrics, StorifyMe and minute-ly code was served to visitors of major websites including BBC, Zoom, HSBC UAE and Fox Sports. The injected code carries a browser-based financial-theft module that substitutes cryptocurrency addresses and includes card-skimming behavior. The same delivery channel also routes to iPhone exploit-kit stages linked to Coruna and DarkSword, though these are delivery observations rather than proven device compromises. Audience figures for the affected sites are context only and do not measure victims, and the number of affected visitors or successful thefts remains unknown. Defenders should remove the poisoned code, block both delivery paths, and treat blocking domains alone as insufficient because some specimens embed a full fallback payload.",
