      "report_date": "2026-11-16",
      "title": "GzipGnaw ClickFix kit",
      "summary": "GzipGnaw is a ClickFix loader that stores its next stage encrypted and compressed in an Ethereum Sepolia contract, a technique known as EtherHiding. It has been matched on 6,443 sites since 3 August, with 2,706 matches in the last 30 days as of 25 November 2026. The loader fetches the contract's bytes, decrypts and decompresses them in the browser, and runs the result, while caching responses in local storage. Some sites also carry a misspelled fake tag manager script, goolgetagmanager.js. Of 1,042 sites recaptured at least 25 days after first match, 69% were still serving it, and 95% of recent sites run WordPress.",
