      "title": "ChainBite ClickFix kit",
      "summary": "ChainBite is a ClickFix kit that splits its attack across multiple BNB Smart Chain testnet contracts, with each contract handling one stage. The injected loader fetches the next stage from these contracts, which return a hostname or script depending on the build, and then selects a Windows or macOS lure by operating system. The lure tracks visitors on-chain using a cjs_id cookie and a yes/no contract, hiding the fake check from those who already ran the command. Lure commands on Windows chain pcalua.exe, curl, and regsvr32 to run a scriptlet via Squiblydoo. Researchers file this activity under ClearFake, and defenders can check page source for injected data URI scripts, a load_ function, or the cjs_id cookie.",
