      "title": "LenAI ClickFix kit",
      "summary": "LenAI is a packed ClickFix loader that reads its controller address from Polygon smart contracts, and it has been matched on 14,723 sites since 1 August. Its code is rented to several operators, and a stage that removes rival loaders and wallet drainers from infected pages has been seen since 28 September. Most infections sit inline in or appended to WordPress scripts, with 93% of recent sites running WordPress, and some are placed on bait sites posing as a free PDF editor. The lure poses as a Cloudflare, Microsoft or DDoS-Guard human check and tricks Windows, Mac and Linux users into pasting commands that download and run scripts. Defenders should inspect page source and theme or plugin JavaScript for atob and new Function patterns and wpmbchik markers, and flag browser requests to public Polygon RPC services from sites without blockchain features.",
